   "source": [
    "# Quiz: CartPole Skating\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-2-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Chess and Go are games with continuous states.</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>true</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Chess and Go have a discrete state. CartPole is the problem with a continuous state.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>false</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Chess and Go have a board with given rules and a discrete state, not a continuous one.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-2-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is the CartPole problem?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a process for eliminating outliers</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. CartPole is a balancing problem. The goal is to balance a pole on top of a slider.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a method for optimizing your shopping cart</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The cart is a slider that moves left or right to balance a pole on top.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a simplified version of balancing</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. CartPole is a simplified version of balancing a pole on a slider that moves left or right.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-2-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What tool can we use to play out different scenarios of potential states in a game?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>guess and check</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The tool for this is a simulation environment, like OpenAI Gym, which simulates the game for you.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>simulation environments</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A simulation environment, like OpenAI Gym, can simulate many games, from cartpole to Atari games.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>state transition testing</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The tool for this is a simulation environment, like OpenAI Gym, which simulates the game for you.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-2-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Where do we define all possible actions in an environment?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>methods</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The possible actions are defined by the environment's action space.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>action space</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Each environment has an action space that defines the possible actions.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>action list</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The right term is action space, which defines the possible actions.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-2-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What pair did we use as the dictionary key-value?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>(state, action) as the key, Q-Table entry as the value</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. The key was the pair (state, action), and the value was the Q-Table entry.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>state as the key, action as the value</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The key was the pair (state, action), not the state alone. The value was the Q-Table entry.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>the value of the qvalues function as the key, action as the value</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. qvalues() only returns the Q-Table values for a state. The key was the pair (state, action).</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-2-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What are the hyperparameters we used during Q-Learning?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>q-table value, current reward, random action</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The hyperparameters were alpha, gamma and epsilon: the learning rate, discount factor and exploration/exploitation factor.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>learning rate, discount factor, exploration/exploitation factor</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Alpha is the learning rate, gamma is the discount factor, and epsilon is the exploration/exploitation factor.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>cumulative rewards, learning rate, exploration factor</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Cumulative reward is a result collected during training. The third hyperparameter is the discount factor.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
